hana: quick thread 1486 - i'm updating the troubleshooting reference for 429s, timeouts, and context errors. PR: https://git.redwood/docs/pull/512. need 2 quick reviews: SDK snippets and the migration note for silent-trim -> explicit error.

ryan: i'll check the python snippet. make sure we show honoring Retry-After and a graceful fallback to a compatible model after repeated 429s. also add a tiny note about not retrying forever (max_attempts).

hana: agreed. also we should fix one broken internal link i found to the old rate-limit playbook.

oliver: wording nit: don't say "smaller model" 1 say "compatible variant" and mention policy gating (fallback only when variant exists in catalog).

keisha: added a compact JS example in the PR showing exponential backoff + retry-after + model swap after 3 attempts. pasted below.

keisha: ```js
// compact JS retry example
async function sendWithRetries(client, opts) {
  const MAX = 5;
  let attempts = 0;
  let model = opts.model || 'redwood-standard-v1';
  while (attempts < MAX) {
    try {
      return await client.generate({ ...opts, model });
    } catch (e) {
      if (e.status === 429) {
        const ra = parseInt(e.headers?.['retry-after'] || '1', 10);
        const wait = Math.min(10000, 300 * 2 ** attempts) + ra * 1000;
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait));
        if (attempts >= 2) model = 'redwood-compat-quant-v1';
        attempts++;
        continue;
      }
      if (e.code === 'CONTEXT_WINDOW_EXCEEDED') {
        throw new Error('CONTEXT_WINDOW_EXCEEDED - recommend truncation or KV cache');
      }
      throw e;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('max retries reached');
}
```

ryan: LGTM, just change MAX to 6 and add a one-line migration callout: "Older SDKs silently trimmed context; current runtime returns CONTEXT_WINDOW_EXCEEDED. Update clients to present an error or apply explicit truncation/KV cache."

